1
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:52,890
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:55,810
[Episode 3]

3
00:01:10,550 --> 00:01:11,810
It's me! It's me!

4
00:01:13,289 --> 00:01:14,789
I'm San Yan'er.

5
00:01:15,930 --> 00:01:16,980
Just kidding.

6
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:35,860
Yang.

7
00:01:35,950 --> 00:01:37,259
You almost choked me to death.

8
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:40,030
I was startled when I saw you just now.

9
00:01:40,210 --> 00:01:41,570
I thought I'd seen a ghost.

10
00:01:45,670 --> 00:01:46,880
Aren't you afraid of ghosts?

11
00:01:47,060 --> 00:01:47,870
What's there to be afraid of?

12
00:01:47,870 --> 00:01:48,680
You're my brother.

13
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:50,140
Even if you're dead,
you're still my brother.

14
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:52,000
They said the big fire at the forest farm

15
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,210
burned quite a few people to death.

16
00:01:53,710 --> 00:01:54,620
I was so worried.

17
00:01:54,620 --> 00:01:55,810
I was worried you didn't make it out.

18
00:01:58,070 --> 00:01:58,640
Really?

19
00:01:58,870 --> 00:02:00,350
Of course.

20
00:02:00,350 --> 00:02:01,760
We're brothers
who've been through life and death.

21
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:02,850
Your parents are my parents.

22
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:04,210
And my parents are your parents.

23
00:02:04,650 --> 00:02:05,710
What's wrong?

24
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:09,500
Why the long face?
Not even a hint of a smile.

25
00:02:10,039 --> 00:02:10,889
Smile.

26
00:02:11,570 --> 00:02:12,950
You're not happy to see me?

27
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:13,690
Brother.

28
00:02:14,250 --> 00:02:14,960
Smile.

29
00:02:15,630 --> 00:02:16,620
We were so close when we were kids.

30
00:02:16,620 --> 00:02:17,710
Smile.

31
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,180
Give me a smile.

32
00:02:20,460 --> 00:02:21,500
Come on.

33
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:22,860
Smile.

34
00:02:24,710 --> 00:02:25,900
Smile.

35
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:34,620
That's much better.

36
00:02:34,829 --> 00:02:37,150
Why always the long face? Really.

37
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:39,430
Did you bring cigarettes?

38
00:02:41,210 --> 00:02:42,740
You're the slickest one.

39
00:02:52,460 --> 00:02:53,460
Three five.

40
00:02:53,810 --> 00:02:54,630
555.

41
00:02:57,530 --> 00:02:58,579
Marlboro.

42
00:02:58,579 --> 00:02:59,520
Marlboro.

43
00:03:03,630 --> 00:03:04,650
Dunhill.

44
00:03:05,850 --> 00:03:06,790
Dunhill.

45
00:03:06,820 --> 00:03:08,150
This is the best one.

46
00:03:09,130 --> 00:03:10,400
My grandpa was paralyzed.

47
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:11,930
After smoking it, he suddenly stood up.

48
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:14,970
That's better. You're smiling.

49
00:03:15,430 --> 00:03:16,630
Do you know what I do now?

50
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:17,210
What do you do?

51
00:03:17,210 --> 00:03:20,000
I'm all knives, guns, and firepower.

52
00:03:20,650 --> 00:03:21,680
I'm a man of the streets.

53
00:03:22,750 --> 00:03:24,780
Half the cigarettes in Tiecheng
go out through my mouth.

54
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:26,240
No, through my hands.

55
00:03:26,930 --> 00:03:28,370
I'm awesome now.

56
00:03:29,310 --> 00:03:30,150
Why aren't you smoking?

57
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:31,500
It's too expensive.

58
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:32,900
I can't afford it.

59
00:03:34,150 --> 00:03:35,800
Forget it then. I'll smoke later.

60
00:03:38,690 --> 00:03:39,960
When did you come back?

61
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:42,860
A couple of days ago.

62
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:45,590
And you've been staying here?

63
00:03:49,590 --> 00:03:51,740
Just staying here
to have some peace and quiet first.

64
00:03:53,130 --> 00:03:53,800
Brother.

65
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,740
Won't you get bloated like this?

66
00:03:56,329 --> 00:03:56,970
Come with me.

67
00:03:57,430 --> 00:03:58,150
Let's go to my place.

68
00:03:58,590 --> 00:03:59,500
We haven't seen each other for so long.

69
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:00,360
I'll talk your ear off.

70
00:04:01,590 --> 00:04:02,180
Let's go.

71
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:04,960
Do you live alone?

72
00:04:05,710 --> 00:04:06,590
I'm a man of the streets.

73
00:04:06,590 --> 00:04:07,740
How could I live alone?

74
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:08,810
Are you kidding?

75
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:10,400
So you have a girlfriend?

76
00:04:10,710 --> 00:04:11,750
And my mom.

77
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:15,900
My mom is streetwise too.

78
00:04:16,209 --> 00:04:17,370
And my elder sister.

79
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:19,500
I have my own room. Let's go.

80
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:20,500
Forget it.

81
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:22,600
I've booked this room for the night.

82
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:23,630
How about this?

83
00:04:23,630 --> 00:04:26,000
I'll go find you
first thing tomorrow morning, okay?

84
00:04:26,250 --> 00:04:27,690
Let's go, brother.

85
00:04:27,690 --> 00:04:29,000
Come on. Hurry up. Let's go.

86
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,130
I've already booked this room.

87
00:04:30,130 --> 00:04:31,510
Just wait... wait until tomorrow morning.

88
00:04:31,510 --> 00:04:32,740
What is a brother?

89
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:34,730
It's seeing you in a swamp

90
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:36,010
and pulling you right out.

91
00:04:36,010 --> 00:04:36,630
Let's go, brother.

92
00:04:36,630 --> 00:04:37,980
I can't pretend I didn't see you.

93
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:39,100
Come on. Hurry up and come with me.

94
00:04:39,870 --> 00:04:40,540
We're brothers.

95
00:04:40,540 --> 00:04:41,330
Let's go, let's go.

96
00:04:42,570 --> 00:04:44,430
Your brother here is different now.

97
00:04:44,930 --> 00:04:46,430
Do you know what they call me out there?

98
00:04:46,770 --> 00:04:47,830
Brother Yan'er.

99
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:49,630
What Yan'er? Asshole?

100
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:51,460
What kind of talk is that?

101
00:04:51,620 --> 00:04:52,450
Hurry up, asshole.

102
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:54,620
With that attitude of yours,

103
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:56,250
you'll have to call me
Master Yan'er from now on.

104
00:04:57,390 --> 00:04:58,120
Master Yan'er.

105
00:04:58,120 --> 00:04:59,659
If I call you, will you answer?

106
00:04:59,980 --> 00:05:01,250
Of course I will.

107
00:05:01,250 --> 00:05:02,750
Who wouldn't be happy
to have another grandson?

108
00:05:02,750 --> 00:05:03,800
Asshole, little asshole.

109
00:05:03,850 --> 00:05:05,690
What did you say?
Don't gross me out, okay?

110
00:05:09,930 --> 00:05:10,500
Come on.

111
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:12,770
I won't. I won't.

112
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:14,010
These past few years,

113
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:16,160
I've also trained

114
00:05:16,270 --> 00:05:17,660
with the Tiecheng Ballet Troupe.

115
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:20,100
You want me to step on the manhole cover?

116
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:21,130
I won't.

117
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:22,710
I won't.

118
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:25,290
I won't.

119
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:28,560
Screw you.

120
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:33,740
Hey, you think you're grabbing your son?

121
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:34,540
The bag dropped.

122
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:35,420
Hurry, pick it up.

123
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:37,540
You carry it for me, little asshole.

124
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:41,940
Screw you.

125
00:05:42,950 --> 00:05:43,370
Okay, okay.

126
00:05:43,370 --> 00:05:44,540
I'll carry it, I'll carry it.

127
00:05:44,980 --> 00:05:46,930
Always fooling around. No sense of limits.

128
00:05:50,190 --> 00:05:51,600
Weren't you pretty reckless
when you were a kid?

129
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:52,810
Jumping on manhole covers.

130
00:05:53,390 --> 00:05:54,740
Not as reckless as you.

131
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:57,650
You know what?

132
00:05:58,430 --> 00:05:59,500
Now that you mention it, I remember.

133
00:06:00,570 --> 00:06:01,980
When I was a kid, I fell into a cesspit.

134
00:06:04,190 --> 00:06:05,870
I just fell right in.

135
00:06:06,430 --> 00:06:07,540
And my mind went blank.

136
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:11,160
Those bastard classmates all left.

137
00:06:12,070 --> 00:06:12,740
Only you

138
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:16,480
jumped in and pulled me out.

139
00:06:17,860 --> 00:06:18,870
If it weren't for you,

140
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,720
I would have died in the cesspit
feeding maggots, brother.

141
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:23,660
Stop, brother. That's too disgusting.

142
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,070
No.

143
00:06:26,060 --> 00:06:27,720
I owe you my life, Yang.

144
00:06:28,860 --> 00:06:30,360
We're brothers
who were in the same cesspit.

145
00:06:31,310 --> 00:06:32,630
You go live with shit.

146
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:34,400
Go live with shit yourself.

147
00:06:34,450 --> 00:06:36,010
Your attitude is a bit too much.

148
00:06:39,180 --> 00:06:39,770
Here.

149
00:06:50,340 --> 00:06:51,550
It's not your home?

150
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,240
Everyone's asleep.

151
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:57,420
Shh.

152
00:07:48,550 --> 00:07:49,170
Yang.

153
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:53,620
How did you escape the forest fire?

154
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:56,870
Some people in your depot died, right?

155
00:08:00,310 --> 00:08:01,160
I saw you

156
00:08:01,750 --> 00:08:02,870
twitching in your sleep

157
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:05,160
in the bathhouse.

158
00:08:07,650 --> 00:08:08,760
What exactly happened?

159
00:08:17,770 --> 00:08:19,060
I was lucky.

160
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:22,810
When the fire started,

161
00:08:24,190 --> 00:08:24,930
our foreman

162
00:08:24,930 --> 00:08:27,070
led us to retreat along the railway.

163
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:29,980
When I went back to the equipment room
to get tools,

164
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:33,130
a shelf collapsed and knocked me out.

165
00:08:34,010 --> 00:08:35,870
They left without me.

166
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:39,860
Those bastards.

167
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:42,940
And then?

168
00:08:49,390 --> 00:08:50,600
Then...

169
00:08:53,510 --> 00:08:55,270
I heard it from the police.

170
00:08:58,840 --> 00:09:00,360
The wind changed direction
in the middle of the night.

171
00:09:02,530 --> 00:09:04,320
The fire didn't come toward the station.

172
00:09:06,530 --> 00:09:07,870
So I got lucky and survived.

173
00:09:13,650 --> 00:09:15,030
The foreman and the others...

174
00:09:16,340 --> 00:09:17,860
were smothered by the fire on the railway

175
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:19,050
and burned to ashes.

176
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:22,890
That's karma.

177
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:24,750
Yang.

178
00:09:26,290 --> 00:09:28,860
You're a good person, so you survived.

179
00:09:29,510 --> 00:09:32,170
They were bad people, so they died.

180
00:09:32,460 --> 00:09:33,720
They deserved to burn to death.

181
00:09:37,170 --> 00:09:38,460
If I tell you...

182
00:09:41,290 --> 00:09:44,080
I never escaped the fire that day,

183
00:09:47,790 --> 00:09:48,720
would you believe me?

184
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:01,340
What?

185
00:10:03,980 --> 00:10:04,740
Brother.

186
00:10:10,510 --> 00:10:12,480
I think I'm already dead.

187
00:10:21,890 --> 00:10:24,130
Every time I close my eyes now,

188
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:30,650
I feel like I'm engulfed in flames,

189
00:10:34,510 --> 00:10:36,630
burning and sizzling.

190
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:40,240
Maybe that day,

191
00:10:41,510 --> 00:10:43,630
some desperate wild beast,

192
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:47,720
with nowhere to hide from the fire,

193
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:54,500
crawled into this body of mine.

194
00:10:57,840 --> 00:10:59,360
Otherwise, I wouldn't...

195
00:10:59,360 --> 00:10:59,980
Yang.

196
00:11:05,530 --> 00:11:07,250
People who survive a disaster
are all like this.

197
00:11:08,530 --> 00:11:09,510
Let's not think about it.

198
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:13,460
Even if you're a ghost,

199
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:15,580
you're still my brother.

200
00:11:16,130 --> 00:11:16,980
Don't worry.

201
00:11:18,250 --> 00:11:20,720
I'll definitely warm your heart up.

202
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:23,130
You can eat,

203
00:11:23,130 --> 00:11:24,890
get married, and have kids as normal.

204
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:26,390
Let's not think about it.

205
00:11:28,410 --> 00:11:29,600
You were just scared.

206
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:32,130
Let's not think about it. Come on.

207
00:11:45,040 --> 00:11:48,690
[Yuhong Square Police Station]

208
00:12:40,770 --> 00:12:43,140
[Yuhong Stadium]

209
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:56,130
What kind of junk is this?
It's broken again.

210
00:13:13,290 --> 00:13:14,570
Who was that quick?

211
00:13:14,970 --> 00:13:16,550
Building a snowman here
right after it started snowing.

212
00:13:25,020 --> 00:13:25,950
It's a person.

213
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:30,120
Are you asleep?

214
00:13:30,910 --> 00:13:31,720
Wake up.

215
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:46,600
Dispatch, dispatch.

216
00:13:47,070 --> 00:13:48,370
This is the Yuhong Square Police Station.

217
00:13:48,930 --> 00:13:50,570
Someone is frozen at the stadium.

218
00:14:52,050 --> 00:14:53,620
There's water in the thermos on the table.

219
00:17:13,440 --> 00:17:15,950
I heard that Juan
from the Yuhong Square Police Station

220
00:17:16,020 --> 00:17:18,880
got a formal reprimand from the bureau
because of him.

221
00:17:18,940 --> 00:17:21,240
Exactly. What rotten luck.

222
00:17:21,740 --> 00:17:23,660
What should we do? He's frozen stiff.

223
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:25,480
The sub-bureau is waiting for the report.

224
00:17:25,660 --> 00:17:26,540
Mentor,

225
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:28,750
how about... blowing on him?

226
00:17:29,210 --> 00:17:30,580
With your mouth?

227
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:38,110
I think
you're about to get reprimanded too.
